# ── Phase-13 — TAIL CALLS (the tail-call proposal: return_call 0x12 / return_call_indirect 0x13).
#    Lowered to GENUINE constant-stack BEAM tail calls (direct reuses the KReturn tail path; indirect
#    goes through the `rt_table.call_indirect_lookup` seam then tail-applies the package-ABI target;
#    imported reuses the import path under KReturn — value-correct/bounded-frame). At wabt 1.0.41 the
#    tail-call opcode is NOT default-on, so `wast2json` needs the trailing FLAG COLUMN
#    `--enable-tail-call` (measured: bare conversion errors "opcode not allowed: return_call"). Both
#    files self-consistency-check under `spectest-interp --enable-tail-call` (47/47, 79/79). The single
#    `spectest.print_i32_f32` host tail call in each is a categorized skip under the deny-all Safe host
#    (a POLICY denial, not a spec trap — it PASSES under the open-host `unsafe` profile).
return_call	--enable-tail-call
return_call_indirect	--enable-tail-call

